 \subsection{Hardware-Software Security Contracts}\label{sec:bg-contracts}
 Hardware-software security contracts~\cite{guarnieri2021contracts} specify which executions of a victim program an attacker may distinguish through hardware side channels. A contract pairs an \emph{observer mode}, which defines what architectural state each execution step exposes, with an \emph{execution mode}, which defines the paths along which the program exposes it~\cite[\S III-B]{guarnieri2021contracts}. Two observer modes capture standard assumptions about software~\cite{guarnieri2021contracts,cauligi2022sok}: \contract{CT} exposes the program counter and the addresses of loads and stores, modeling constant-time code, and \contract{ARCH} also exposes every loaded value, modeling code that never accesses secrets architecturally. The \contract{SEQ} execution mode collects observations only along the sequential path.
 % , while \contract{COND} also follows mispredicted branches~\cite{revizor}. 
